# Witnesses for all derived-overlap extensions

The overlap is generated by rows 1 and 2, of orders eight and two. Their
images are detected by nontrivial fourth power, trivial square, and trivial
fourth power of their product. There are 32 possible pairs. Each has a permutation of the 96
left-parabolic rows extending it. The inverse permutations are supplied too.
`Checks` verifies the data against the previously realized word table.

